   <media:title>Remembering those who lost their lives in the Aberfan disaster</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/c1gkvHEWk88?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/c1gkvHEWk88/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>Sixty years on, we remember the 144 people who lost their lives in the Aberfan disaster. 
 
Today, The King and The Queen, with The Prince of Wales, spent time at the Aberfan Memorial Garden and the Aberfan and Merthyr Vale Community Centre to honour their memory.
 
The Aberfan Memorial Garden stands on the site of Pantglas School, where 109 children and 5 teachers died when the coal tip collapsed onto the village.

Watch His Majesty’s speech in full on our YouTube channel (link in bio).</media:description>
