  <media:group>
   <media:title>Finishing touches ahead of tonight’s State Banquet… ✨</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/tEJX__L28ZY?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i1.ytimg.com/vi/tEJX__L28ZY/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>Tonight, The King and Queen will host a State Banquet for the Sultan of Oman at Windsor Castle.
 
Inspired by the Omani ritual of Kahwa, a collection of special teas will be served.
 
While Kahwa is traditionally a spiced coffee, the concept has been adapted to draw on the long-standing British love of tea while preserving the aromatic spices and flavours that make Kahwa so distinctive: fragrant cardamom, delicate rose, sweet dates, and gentle warming spices.
 
Guests will be invited to choose from an Iced Earl Grey &amp; Date, an Iced Mint &amp; Rose, or a Warm Cardamom-Spiced Blend sweetened with Windsor Honey.
 
Together, they reflect the warmth and hospitality shared by both Omani and British traditions.</media:description>
